From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:52:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: lay out ucontext_t as the kernel writes it

The wasm kernel uses asm-generic's struct ucontext: uc_flags, uc_link,
uc_stack, uc_mcontext, then uc_sigmask. musl's wasm ucontext_t had no
uc_flags and put uc_sigmask second, so a handler that read or changed
its context touched the wrong fields. The cancellation handler's
addition of SIGCANCEL to the mask sigreturn restores never reached the
mask, and its re-raised SIGCANCEL was delivered again at every
sigreturn, without end.
---
diff --git a/arch/wasm/bits/signal.h b/arch/wasm/bits/signal.h
index ab24d3d..5b96b5f 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/bits/signal.h
+++ b/arch/wasm/bits/signal.h
@@ -29,11 +29,13 @@ struct sigaltstack {
 	size_t ss_size;
 };
 
+/* the kernel's asm-generic struct ucontext, which its signal frame and rt_sigreturn use */
 typedef struct __ucontext {
+	unsigned long uc_flags;
 	struct __ucontext *uc_link;
-	sigset_t uc_sigmask;
 	stack_t uc_stack;
 	mcontext_t uc_mcontext;
+	sigset_t uc_sigmask;
 } ucontext_t;
 
 #define SA_NOCLDSTOP  1
